The Mercedes-Benz C-Class C300h is a diesel hybrid variant from the W205 generation, produced from 2014 to 2018 (Source [1, 7, 8, 41]). It combines a 2.1L 4-cylinder diesel engine with an electric motor. This evaluation is based on the W205 C300h relative to the current automotive market.

*   **price\_usd**: As a used car from 2014-2018, the price is significantly lower than a new car today. Used prices in the UK can be found from around £9,293 to £13,736 (approx $11,700 - $17,300 USD) (Source [25, 27]). This is well below the $35,000 average for a new car. Score: 0.80.
*   **total\_cost\_estimate\_5yr\_usd**: While the purchase price is low, an older luxury hybrid car will have higher maintenance and potential repair costs than a new economy car (Source [9, 16]). The hybrid components could add complexity and expense. Score: -0.40.
*   **insurance\_usd\_yr**: Insurance groups for the W205 C300h were in the higher mid-range for its time (Group 37 in the UK) (Source [32, 35]). Relative to modern cars, this is likely around average or slightly above. Score: 0.00.
*   **maint\_usd\_yr**: Maintenance costs for a Mercedes-Benz are generally higher than average (Source [9, 16, 39]). The added complexity of a diesel hybrid system could lead to higher maintenance costs. Score: -0.70.
*   **repair\_risk\_score**: The W205 generation had some reported issues, including with the M274 petrol engine (wrist pin/piston issues on early C300 models, though the C300h uses a diesel engine) (Source [10, 16, 34, 40]). The OM651 diesel engine is generally considered reliable, but the hybrid system adds potential points of failure (Source [16]). CarEdge rates the W205 C-Class as worse than average for major repair probability over 10 years (Source [9]). Score: -0.40.
*   **hp**: Combined system output is 228-231 hp (Source [1, 2, 3, 7, 8, 41]). This is above the 200 hp average. Score: 0.20.
*   **torque**: Combined system torque is 500 Nm (368.78 lb-ft) or 750 Nm (553.17 lb-ft) depending on how it's measured (engine vs system peak) (Source [1, 2, 3, 38, 41]). Using the higher system peak torque. This is significantly above the 190 lb-ft average. Score: 0.90.
*   **cylinder\_count**: The internal combustion engine is a 4-cylinder diesel (Source [1, 2, 3, 7, 8, 38, 41]). This is common, so average. Score: 0.00.
*   **engine\_displacement**: The internal combustion engine is 2.1L (2143 cm³) (Source [1, 2, 3, 38, 41]). Around the average for a 4-cylinder engine. Score: 0.00.
*   **accel\_0\_60\_sec**: Around 6.1-6.9 seconds (0-100 km/h in 6.4-7.2s) (Source [1, 3, 8, 33, 41]). This is significantly faster than the 7.5-second average. Score: 0.60.
*   **top\_speed**: Around 151-152 mph (244 km/h) (Source [1, 2, 8, 41]). Around the 150 mph average. Score: 0.00.
*   **drive\_type**: RWD (Source [1, 2, 7, 8, 41]). Score: 1.00 (based on guide).
*   **transmission\_type**: 7-speed automatic (7G-TRONIC PLUS) (Source [1, 2, 3, 8, 38, 41]). A modern automatic for its time. Score: 1.00.
*   **offroad\_ability**: Low ground clearance (around 92mm or 3.62 inches) (Source [1]), sedan/estate body style, not designed for off-road. Score: 1.00 (based on guide examples).
*   **braking\_dist\_ft**: Not explicitly stated, but expected to be good for its class and era. Score: 0.00.
*   **size**: Length is around 4686 mm (184.5 inches) (Source [1, 3, 4, 5, 13, 19, 41]). Around the 4.6m average. Score: 0.00.
*   **wheelbase**: 2840 mm (111.81 inches) (Source [1, 4, 5, 8, 13, 19, 41]). This is longer than the 2700mm average. Score: 0.20.
*   **body\_style**: Available as Sedan or Estate (Source [1, 7, 8, 19, 20, 21, 32]). Score: 0.00.
*   **seats**: 5 seats (Source [1, 7, 8, 20, 41]). Score: 0.00.
*   **cargo\_space**: 435 liters (15.36 cu ft) for the sedan (Source [1, 20, 41]). The battery reduces trunk space compared to the standard W205 sedan (480 liters / 16.95 cu ft) (Source [4]). This is around the 15 cu ft average. Score: 0.00.
*   **rear\_space**: Improved over the previous W204 generation (Source [11, 33]). Score: 0.00.
*   **ground\_clearance\_in**: Around 92mm (3.62 inches) (Source [1]). Low for a sedan by modern standards. Score: -0.20.
*   **turn\_radius\_ft**: Around 11.22m (36.81 ft) (Source [1, 4]). Around the 36 ft average. Score: 0.00.
*   **mpg**: Hybrid system provides excellent fuel economy. Claimed combined around 3.6-4.0 L/100 km (58.8 - 65.34 US mpg, 70.62 - 78.47 UK mpg) (Source [1]). Real-world MPG is often lower but still very good (around 37-58 mpg Real MPG, 50.2 mpg average) (Source [12]). This is well above the 30 mpg average for a conventional car. Score: 0.80.
*   **co2\_g\_km**: Around 94-99 g/km (Source [1]). This is well below the 175 g/km average. Score: 0.80.
*   **electric\_range\_mi**: As a full hybrid (FHEV), it has a small battery and limited electric-only range, typically only a few miles at low speeds (Source [37, 38]). Score: 0.00.
*   **charge\_speed\_kw**: Not a plug-in hybrid, so no external charging capability. Score: -1.00.
*   **style\_sleek\_vs\_boxy**: W205 design is a sleek, modern sedan shape, inspired by the S-Class (Source [11, 29, 37]). Score: 0.40.
*   **style\_aggression\_rating**: Standard C-Class styling is elegant, AMG Line adds aggression (Source [15, 20]). Assuming standard C300h styling. Score: 0.00.
*   **style\_modernity\_rating**: Design is from the mid-2010s. Looks somewhat dated compared to the current W206, but still reasonably modern. Score: -0.20.
*   **handling\_rating**: Generally competent handling, described as comfortable and refined rather than overtly sporty (Source [11, 27, 33]). Score: 0.00.
*   **ride\_comfort\_rating**: Praised for a superb ride quality, even with sport suspension (Source [11, 33, 37]). Score: 0.80.
*   **cabin\_noise\_rating**: Incredibly quiet and refined, especially at motorway speeds (Source [11, 37]). Score: 0.80.
*   **shift\_smooth\_rating**: 7G-Tronic Plus is generally smooth (Source [37]). The transition between electric and diesel power can sometimes be noticeable or jarring (Source [37]). Score: 0.00.
*   **steering\_feel\_rating**: Reviews often noted a lack of steering feel (Source [11]). Score: -0.50.
*   **adas\_score**: Offered a good range of ADAS for its time, including Collision Prevention Assist and a reversing camera as standard (Source [11, 20]). Optional features like Distronic Plus were available. Score: 0.20.
*   **visibility\_rating**: Standard sedan visibility. Score: 0.00.
*   **headlight\_rating**: LED headlights were available (Source [20]). Good for their time, but not modern adaptive matrix LEDs. Score: 0.20.
*   **security\_rating**: Standard for a luxury car of its time, with alarm and immobiliser (Source [20]). Score: 0.00.
*   **screen\_in**: Featured a tablet-style screen, typically around 7-8.4 inches with COMAND Online (Source [11]). Average for its time, but small by modern standards. Score: -0.20.
*   **infotainment\_ux\_rating**: COMAND Online was advanced for its time, but the interface is less intuitive than modern systems (Source [11]). Score: -0.20.
*   **smartphone\_connect\_rating**: Bluetooth, USB, and a media interface were standard (Source [11, 20]). Apple CarPlay/Android Auto were introduced later in the W205's life, possibly not standard on early C300h models. Score: -0.50.
*   **audio\_rating**: Optional Burmester system was excellent (Source [20]). Standard system is likely average. Score: 0.00.
*   **usb\_ports**: Likely one or two ports. Score: -0.50.
*   **comfort\_feature\_score**: Heated front seats, power seats, dual-zone climate control, ambient lighting available (Source [20]). Good level of comfort features for its era. Score: 0.40.
*   **convenience\_feature\_score**: Auto parking, blind-spot sensor, driver attention detection, reversing camera standard (Source [20]). Lacks some modern convenience tech like 360 cameras as standard. Score: 0.20.
*   **brand\_prestige\_rating**: Mercedes-Benz is a high-prestige brand. Score: 0.80.
*   **model\_prestige\_rating**: C-Class is a core, mid-range model for Mercedes-Benz. Score: 0.00.
*   **trim\_prestige\_rating**: C300h was a higher-end engine variant focusing on efficiency and technology, but not a full AMG performance model. Score: -0.20.
*   **interior\_luxury\_rating**: W205 interior was a significant improvement in quality and design over the W204, feeling very premium for its time (Source [11, 33, 37]). Materials and design are somewhat dated compared to the latest luxury interiors. Score: 0.50.
*   **interior\_tech\_focus\_rating**: Featured a prominent screen and COMAND Online, representing a good tech focus for its era, but less screen-dominated than the current W206. Score: 0.20.

